zΔ⚡b|=36dd|+ editor)%7Ced]] script can be generated by modern versions of diff with the <code>%2De</code> option. The resulting edit script for this example is as follows:%0A%0A 24'''a'''%0A %0A ''This paragraph contains''%0A ''important new additions''%0A ''to this document.''%0A .%0A 17'''c'''%0A ''check this document. On''%0A .%0A 11,15'''d'''%0A 0'''a'''%0A ''This is an important''%0A ''notice! It should''%0A ''therefore be locate|=cf|+ containing a <code>w</code> (write) command, and one containing a <code>q</code> (quit) command (e.g. by {{code%7Clang%3Dbash%7Cprintf "w\nq\n" >> mydiff}}). Here we gave the diff file the name ''mydiff'' and the transformation will then happen when we run {{code%7Clang%3Dbash%7Ced %2Ds original < mydiff}}.|=e5|+2.8 BSD, released in July 1981. The context format of diff introduced at Berkeley|=19c|+file and find the intended location for a change to be applied regardless of whether the line|=1a|+ The |=23c|-1|+.%0A%0A|=9a|+%7C%2D}}" the removal of a line. A blank [[space (punctua|=5|+%7Cspace]] represents a|=1ef|+diff %2Dc original new}} produces the following output:%0A<syntaxhighlight lang%3D"diff">%0A*** /path/to/original%09timestamp%0A%2D%2D%2D /path/to/new%09timestamp%0A***************%0A*** 1,3 ****%0A%2D%2D%2D 1,9 %2D%2D%2D%2D%0A%2B This is an important%0A%2B notice! It should%0A%2B therefore be located at%0A%2B the beginning of this%0A%2B document!%0A%2B%0A  This part of the%0A  document has stayed the%0A  same from version to%0A***************%0A*** 8,20 ****%0A  compress the size of the%0A  changes.%0A%0A%2D This paragraph contains%0A%2D text that is outdated.%0A%2D It will be deleted in the%0A%2D near future.%0A%0A  It is important to spell%0A! check this dokument. On%0A  the other hand, a%0A  misspelled word isn't%0A  the end of the world.%0A%2D%2D%2D 14,21 %2D%2D%2D%2D%0A  compress the size of the%0A  changes.%0A%0A  It is important to spell%0A! check this document. On%0A  the other hand, a%0A  misspelled word isn't%0A  the end of the world.%0A***************%0A*** 22,24 ****%0A%2D%2D%2D 23,29 %2D%2D%2D%2D%0A  this paragraph needs to%0A  be changed. Things can%0A  be added after it.%0A%2B%0A%2B This paragraph contains%0A%2B important new additions%0A%2B to this document.%0A</syntaxhighlight>|=29fa|+source. It is also used by revision control systems, e.g. [[Revision Control System%7CRCS]], for [[merge (revision control)%7Cmerging]].<ref>{{cite web%7Curl%3Dhttps://www.gnu.org/software/rcs/manual/html_node/merge.html%7Ctitle%3Dmerge (GNU RCS 5.10.0)%7Cwebsite%3Dgnu.org%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D22 January 2021%7Carchive%2Ddate%3D18 September 2019%7Carchive%2Durl%3Dhttps://web.archive.org/web/20190918125803/http://www.gnu.org/software/rcs/manual/html_node/merge.html%7Curl%2Dstatus%3Dlive}}</ref>%0A%0A[[Emacs]] has [[Ediff]] for showing the changes a patch would provide in a user interface that combines interactive editing and merging capabilities for patch files.%0A%0A[[Vim (text editor)%7CVim]] provides '''vimdiff''' to compare from two to eight files, with differences highlighted in color.<ref>{{Cite web%7Cauthor%2Dlink%3DBram Moolenaar%7Cfirst%3DBram%7Clast%3DMoolenaar%7Curl%3Dhttps://vimhelp.org/diff.txt.html#vimdiff%7Ctitle%3DVim documentation: diff%7Cwebsite%3Dvimdoc.sourceforge.net%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D1 May 2020%7Cquote%3DThe easiest way to start editing in diff mode is with the "vimdiff" command. This starts Vim as usual, and additionally sets up for viewing the differences between the arguments. <code>vimdiff file1 file2 [file3] [file4] [...file8]</code> This is equivalent to: <code>vim %2Dd file1 file2 [file3] [file4] [...file8]</code>%7Carchive%2Ddate%3D16 February 2020%7Carchive%2Durl%3Dhttps://web.archive.org/web/20200216203940/https://vimhelp.org/diff.txt.html#vimdiff%7Curl%2Dstatus%3Dlive}}</ref>%0AWhile historically invoking the diff program, modern vim uses [[git]]'s fork of xdiff library (LibXDiff) code, providing improved speed and functionality.<ref name%3D"brabandt2018">{{Cite web%7Ctitle%3DThe power of diff%7Curl%3Dhttps://vimways.org/2018/the%2Dpower%2Dof%2Ddiff/%7Cdate%3D1 December 2018%7Cwebsite%3DVimways%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D1 May 2020%7Cfirst%3DChristian %7Clast%3DBrabandt%7Curl%2Dstatus%3Dlive%7Carchive%2Durl%3Dhttps://web.archive.org/web/20181202020105/https://vimways.org/2018/the%2Dpower%2Dof%2Ddiff/%7Carchive%2Ddate%3D2 December 2018}}</ref>%0A%0AGNU [[Wdiff]]<ref>{{Cite web%7Curl%3Dhttps://gnu.org/s/wdiff/%7Ctitle%3Dgnu.org%7Cwebsite%3Dgnu.org%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D2020%2D09%2D12%7Carchive%2Ddate%3D2020%2D08%2D11%7Carchive%2Durl%3Dhttps://web.archive.org/web/20200811124535/https://gnu.org/s/wdiff/%7Curl%2Dstatus%3Dlive}}</ref> is a front end to diff that shows the words or phrases that changed in a text document of written language even in the presence of word%2Dwrapping or different column widths.%0A%0Acolordiff is a Perl wrapper for 'diff' and produces the same output but with colorization for added and deleted bits.<ref>{{Cite web%7Curl%3Dhttps://www.colordiff.org/%7Ctitle%3Dcolordiff%7Cwebsite%3Dwww.colordiff.org%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D2018%2D06%2D14%7Carchive%2Ddate%3D2018%2D06%2D14%7Carchive%2Durl%3Dhttps://web.archive.org/web/20180614121429/https://www.colordiff.org/%7Curl%2Dstatus%3Dlive}}</ref> diff%2Dso%2Dfancy and diff%2Dhighlight are newer analogues.<ref>{{cite web %7Ctitle%3Ddiff%2Dso%2Dfancy %7Curl%3Dhttps://github.com/so%2Dfancy/diff%2Dso%2Dfancy %7Cpublisher%3DSo Fancy %7Cdate%3D6 May 2023 %7Caccess%2Ddate%3D8 May 2023 %7Carchive%2Ddate%3D8 May 2023 %7Carchi|=274e|
